# This is a verbatim copy of an upstream release, so git must store it exactly
# as published. Without this, 24 files with CRLF endings (the MSVC project
# files, the API samples, compat/jansson, LICENSE.txt) get normalised to LF on
# add, and the copy stops being byte for byte what upstream shipped, which is
# the one property that makes vendoring worth doing.
* -text
